# Reported translation gaps — 2026-10-25

Requirements **TG01–TG09** cover the owner's nine reported areas: challenge creation, Weekly Rivalry time remaining, biomes, customisation parts, music playback status, achievement tiers/small headings, Store ad status, camera modes, and personal ghosts. **R01/G01/Q01** preserve authoritative data, existing controls, and honest validation.

The affected copy now uses the selected language in French, Spanish, German, Brazilian Portuguese, Japanese, Korean, Dutch, Italian, Finnish, Swedish, and Norwegian Bokmål, alongside English. This task adds 93 directly authored table rows. No translation model, network translation service, or new dependency is used.

The source inventory previously omitted the camera, personal-ghost and customisation data tables. It now includes them and explicitly extracts translated countdown calls from the Rivalry model without extracting its sample driver names. Uppercase biome/part/medal text translates the original source before casing; retained bindings update when the locale changes. Creator biome cards and their selected summary use that same path. Custom editor button drawing translates its caption.

Challenge summaries use whole messages and real plural pairs for selected tracks and per-driver/per-track tries. Track names are inserted verbatim, including a name such as `Language` that also matches a catalogue key. Format-card tooltips translate their constituent sentences. Actual rule values, selection, source receipts and creation authority are unchanged.

Rivalry formats the server-derived day/hour values and closing/settling states. Retained views rebuild on a locale change while preserving selection, scroll and focus through their existing rebuild path; ordinary unchanged-locale score refreshes retain the prior cache path. The clock timer is named for direct regression coverage. Adjacent lead/gap hints also translate full messages. The music player preserves release titles inside translated playing/paused/action text. Store access uses translated ad state and slot plurals from cached entitlements; its unit prices refresh through a bound message without re-fetching products or changing checkout state.

Achievement cards, earned-state headings, next medals, milestone names, category eyebrow and unlocked-medal notifications translate their actual tiers. Progress, unlocks and pin authority are unchanged. Settings uses the existing controls and canonical camera/ghost IDs with translated names and descriptions.

`scripts/translations/ui_gaps.tsv` is the authored source. `scripts/localization.py` and `scripts/test_localization.py` cover the inventory change. The runtime changes are in `game/localization/game_text.gd`, `game/core/app.gd`, `game/editor/editor_button.gd`, `game/race/weekly_rivalry.gd`, and the affected UI scripts. The exact changed-file list, source hashes and task-only review patch are recorded in [report.json](evidence/translation-gaps-2026-10-25/report.json) and `checkpoint.patch` beside it. They use task-start snapshots and exclude other workspace changes; no Git index or owner process was changed.

Validation uses pinned Godot `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf`, `scripts/dev.ps1`, fresh workspace-local `APPDATA` directories, and local service fixtures. Actual commands and final outcomes are in the report. The new `test_translation_gaps.gd` exercises packaged entries and actual controls in all twelve locales, the retained creator picker, Rivalry timer, thumbnail/shelf, music, Store, challenge rules/summary and achievement sheet. German, Finnish, Japanese and Korean camera/ghost sections are also checked at 960×540. Captures under `gl_compatibility-final/` and `mobile-final/` are native desktop screenshots, not physical-device evidence.

The retained localization (60), translations/fonts (290), App (141), results challenge setup (74), achievement detail (758) and Rivalry view (361) regressions pass. Python inventory/authoring suites pass 12 and 7 tests. The broader headless challenge-card suite reports 249 checks/14 failures, and Store reference reports 131/6. The two `probe_translation_gaps_original_*` runners reload the exact task-start production scripts only into disposable process memory and reproduce the same failure messages/counts. Those suites are not claimed as passing; no assertion or tolerance was relaxed.

Initial failures remain in the evidence: restricted Windows execution policy, sandboxed native certificate-store access, an achievement fixture with progress but no saved unlocks, and a retained Rivalry clock using the previous locale. Execution uses the existing process-local PowerShell entry point; native checks ran outside the sandbox with automatic approval. The fixture now includes its real unlocks, and the retained-view bug is fixed. The final clock check targets the named countdown timer directly.

The global catalogue remains incomplete: **36 task-start gaps**, mainly editor copy, remain empty across the eleven translations. The strict full-catalogue completeness check therefore still fails; generation used the existing explicit `--allow-incomplete` development flag. This fix does not label those entries as translated or weaken the release check. Owner language/appearance review and game reload remain. No device attachment check or physical-device test, APK, real authentication/purchase, live data mutation, deployment, or owner-process restart was performed.
